#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-index-pack(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:7
msgid "git-index-pack - Build pack index file for an existing packed archive"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git index-pack' [-v] [-o <index-file>] [--[no-]rev-index] <pack-file>\n"
"'git index-pack' --stdin [--fix-thin] [--keep] [-v] [-o <index-file>]\n"
"\t\t  [--[no-]rev-index] [<pack-file>]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:24
msgid ""
"Reads a packed archive (.pack) from the specified file, builds a pack index "
"file (.idx) for it, and optionally writes a reverse-index (.rev) for the "
"specified pack. The packed archive, together with the pack index, can then "
"be placed in the objects/pack/ directory of a Git repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:28
#, no-wrap
msgid "-v"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:30
msgid "Be verbose about what is going on, including progress status."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "-o <index-file>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:38
msgid ""
"Write the generated pack index into the specified file.  Without this option "
"the name of pack index file is constructed from the name of packed archive "
"file by replacing .pack with .idx (and the program fails if the name of "
"packed archive does not end with .pack)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "--[no-]rev-index"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:45
msgid ""
"When this flag is provided, generate a reverse index (a `.rev` file) "
"corresponding to the given pack. If `--verify` is given, ensure that the "
"existing reverse index is correct. Takes precedence over "
"`pack.writeReverseIndex`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "--stdin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:55
msgid ""
"When this flag is provided, the pack is read from stdin instead and a copy "
"is then written to <pack-file>. If <pack-file> is not specified, the pack is "
"written to objects/pack/ directory of the current Git repository with a "
"default name determined from the pack content.  If <pack-file> is not "
"specified consider using --keep to prevent a race condition between this "
"process and 'git repack'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:56
#, no-wrap
msgid "--fix-thin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:61
msgid ""
"Fix a \"thin\" pack produced by `git pack-objects --thin` (see "
"linkgit:git-pack-objects[1] for details) by adding the excluded objects the "
"deltified objects are based on to the pack. This option only makes sense in "
"conjunction with --stdin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "--keep"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:69
msgid ""
"Before moving the index into its final destination create an empty .keep "
"file for the associated pack file.  This option is usually necessary with "
"--stdin to prevent a simultaneous 'git repack' process from deleting the "
"newly constructed pack and index before refs can be updated to use objects "
"contained in the pack."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "--keep=<msg>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:76
msgid ""
"Like --keep, create a .keep file before moving the index into its final "
"destination.  However, instead of creating an empty file place '<msg>' "
"followed by an LF into the .keep file.  The '<msg>' message can later be "
"searched for within all .keep files to locate any which have outlived their "
"usefulness."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "--index-version=<version>[,<offset>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:81
msgid ""
"This is intended to be used by the test suite only. It allows to force the "
"version for the generated pack index, and to force 64-bit index entries on "
"objects located above the given offset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:82
#, no-wrap
msgid "--strict[=<msg-id>=<severity>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:89
msgid ""
"Die, if the pack contains broken objects or links. An optional "
"comma-separated list of `<msg-id>=<severity>` can be passed to change the "
"severity of some possible issues, e.g., "
"`--strict=\"missingEmail=ignore,badTagName=error\"`. See the entry for the "
"`fsck.<msg-id>` configuration options in linkgit:git-fsck[1] for more "
"information on the possible values of `<msg-id>` and `<severity>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:90
#, no-wrap
msgid "--progress-title"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:92
msgid "For internal use only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:95
msgid ""
"Set the title of the progress bar. The title is \"Receiving objects\" by "
"default and \"Indexing objects\" when `--stdin` is specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "--check-self-contained-and-connected"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:98
msgid "Die if the pack contains broken links. For internal use only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "--fsck-objects[=<msg-id>=<severity>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:105
msgid ""
"Die if the pack contains broken objects, but unlike `--strict`, don't choke "
"on broken links. If the pack contains a tree pointing to a .gitmodules blob "
"that does not exist, prints the hash of that blob (for the caller to check) "
"after the hash that goes into the name of the pack/idx file (see \"Notes\")."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:111
msgid ""
"An optional comma-separated list of `<msg-id>=<severity>` can be passed to "
"change the severity of some possible issues, e.g., "
"`--fsck-objects=\"missingEmail=ignore,badTagName=ignore\"`. See the entry "
"for the `fsck.<msg-id>` configuration options in linkgit:git-fsck[1] for "
"more information on the possible values of `<msg-id>` and `<severity>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:112
#, no-wrap
msgid "--threads=<n>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:121
msgid ""
"Specifies the number of threads to spawn when resolving deltas. This "
"requires that index-pack be compiled with pthreads otherwise this option is "
"ignored with a warning.  This is meant to reduce packing time on "
"multiprocessor machines. The required amount of memory for the delta search "
"window is however multiplied by the number of threads.  Specifying 0 will "
"cause Git to auto-detect the number of CPU's and use maximum 3 threads."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:122
#, no-wrap
msgid "--max-input-size=<size>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:124
msgid "Die, if the pack is larger than <size>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "--object-format=<hash-algorithm>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:130
msgid ""
"Specify the given object format (hash algorithm) for the pack.  The valid "
"values are 'sha1' and (if enabled) 'sha256'.  The default is the algorithm "
"for the current repository (set by `extensions.objectFormat`), or 'sha1' if "
"no value is set or outside a repository."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:132
msgid "This option cannot be used with --stdin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:135
#, no-wrap
msgid "--promisor[=<message>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:142
msgid ""
"Before committing the pack-index, create a .promisor file for this "
"pack. Particularly helpful when writing a promisor pack with --fix-thin "
"since the name of the pack is not final until the pack has been fully "
"written. If a `<message>` is provided, then that content will be written to "
"the .promisor file for future reference. See "
"link:technical/partial-clone.html[partial clone] for more information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:147
msgid ""
"Also, if there are objects in the given pack that references non-promisor "
"objects (in the repo), repacks those non-promisor objects into a promisor "
"pack. This avoids a situation in which a repo has non-promisor objects that "
"are accessible through promisor objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:149
msgid "Requires <pack-file> to not be specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:151
#, no-wrap
msgid "NOTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:159
msgid ""
"Once the index has been created, the hash that goes into the name of the "
"pack/idx file is printed to stdout. If --stdin was also used then this is "
"prefixed by either \"pack\\t\", or \"keep\\t\" if a new .keep file was "
"successfully created. This is useful to remove a .keep file used as a lock "
"to prevent the race with 'git repack' mentioned above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:161
#, no-wrap
msgid "GIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation/git-index-pack.txt:162
msgid "Part of the linkgit:git[1] suite"
msgstr ""
